      "text": "Given the function \\( f(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d \\), we need to determine the value of \\( 8a - 4b + 2c - d \\) using the graph provided. The graph indicates that the function crosses the x-axis at \\( x = 0, 1, \\) and \\( 2 \\). This means the roots of the polynomial are \\( x = 0, x = 1, \\) and \\( x = 2 \\).\n\nBy Vieta's formulas, we know that for a cubic polynomial \\( ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d \\) with roots \\( p, q, \\) and \\( r \\):\n\\[\na + b + c + d = 0,\n\\]\n\\[\nab + bc + ca + d = 0,\n\\]\n\\[\nabc + bcd + cda + dab = -\\frac{c}{a},\n\\]\n\\[\nabcd = -\\frac{d}{a}.\n\\]\n\nGiven the roots \\( x = 0, 1, \\) and \\( 2 \\), we can write the polynomial as:\n\\[\nf(x) = a(x-0)(x-1)(x-2) = a(x-0)(x-1)(x-2) = a(x^3 - 3x^2 + 2x).\n\\]\n\nThus, comparing with \\( f(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d \\), we identify:\n\\[\na = a, \\quad b = -3a, \\quad c = 2a, \\quad d = 0.\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the value of \\( 8a - 4b + 2c - d \\):\n\\[\n8a - 4b + 2c - d = 8a - 4(-3a) + 2(2a) - 0.\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression:\n\\[\n8a + 12a + 4a = 24a.\n\\]\n\nSince the value of \\( a \\) cancels out, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{24}.\n\\]",
