      "text": "To determine the value of \\( 8a - 4b + 2c - d \\) for the polynomial \\( f(x) = ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d \\), let's analyze the given graph step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Identify the points on the graph\nFrom the graph, we observe the following key points:\n- The function \\( f(x) \\) passes through the points \\( (0, d) \\), \\( (1, 0) \\), \\( (2, 0) \\), and \\( (3, 2) \\).\n\n### Step 2: Substitute the points into the polynomial\nUsing the points, we can set up a system of equations to solve for \\( a \\), \\( b \\), \\( c \\), and \\( d \\).\n\n1. For \\( (0, d) \\):\n   \\[\n   f(0) = d = 0 \\implies d = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. For \\( (1, 0) \\):\n   \\[\n   f(1) = a(1)^3 + b(1)^2 + c(1) + d = a + b + c = 0\n   \\]\n   Since \\( d = 0 \\), this simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   a + b + c = 0\n   \\]\n\n3. For \\( (2, 0) \\):\n   \\[\n   f(2) = a(2)^3 + b(2)^2 + c(2) + d = 8a + 4b + 2c = 0\n   \\]\n   Since \\( d = 0 \\), this simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   8a + 4b + 2c = 0 \\implies 4a + 2b + c = 0\n   \\]\n\n4. For \\( (3, 2) \\):\n   \\[\n   f(3) = a(3)^3 + b(3)^2 + c(3) + d = 27a + 9b + 3c = 2\n   \\]\n\n### Step 3: Solve the system of linear equations\nWe have the following system of equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\na + b + c = 0 \\\\\n4a + 2b + c = 0 \\\\\n27a + 9b + 3c = 2\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nFirst, subtract the first equation from the second:\n\\[\n(4a + 2b + c) - (a + b + c) = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n3a + b = 0 \\implies b = -3a\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\( b = -3a \\) into the first equation:\n\\[\na + (-3a) + c = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n-2a + c = 0 \\implies c = 2a\n\\]\n\nNow substitute \\( b = -3a \\) and \\( c = 2a \\) into the third equation:\n\\[\n27a + 9(-3a) + 3(2a) = 2\n\\]\n\\[\n27a - 27a + 6a = 2\n\\]\n\\[\n6a = 2 \\implies a = \\frac{1}{3}\n\\]\n\nUsing \\( a = \\frac{1}{3} \\):\n\\[\nb = -3a = -3 \\left( \\frac{1}{3} \\right) = -1\n\\]\n\\[\nc = 2a = 2 \\left( \\frac{1}{3} \\right) = \\frac{2}{3}\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Calculate \\( 8a - 4b + 2c - d \\)\nSince \\( d = 0 \\):\n\\[\n8a - 4b + 2c - d = 8 \\left( \\frac{1}{3} \\right) - 4(-1) + 2 \\left( \\frac{2}{3} \\right) - 0\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{8}{3} + 4 + \\frac{4}{3}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{8}{3} + \\frac{12}{3} + \\frac{4}{3}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{8 + 12 + 4}{3}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{24}{3}\n\\]\n\\[\n= 8\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( 8a - 4b + 2c - d \\) is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).",
